Use the UWP CreateFile2 shim on every UWP target, not just /ZW builds.

builds/windows/ftsystem.c carries a CreateFileA shim that forwards to
CreateFile2, but it is guarded by _WINRT_DLL. MSVC only predefines that when
compiling with /ZW (C++/CX), which is not how vcpkg builds this C library, so
the shim was never compiled and FT_Stream_Open referenced the real CreateFileA.

That still links for x64-uwp and arm64-uwp, whose WindowsApp.lib exports the
ANSI entry point, but x86's WindowsApp.lib does not export it at all, so
freetype:x86-uwp failed with

    ftsystem.c.obj : error LNK2019: unresolved external symbol _CreateFileA
    freetyped.dll : fatal error LNK1120: 1 unresolved externals

Keying off the app family instead builds the shim for every UWP architecture,
which also puts all of them on the same code path. Every API the shim needs
(CreateFile2, CreateFileMappingFromApp, MapViewOfFileFromApp, GetFileSizeEx,
MultiByteToWideChar) is present in the x86 WindowsApp.lib.

diff --git a/builds/windows/ftsystem.c b/builds/windows/ftsystem.c
--- a/builds/windows/ftsystem.c
+++ b/builds/windows/ftsystem.c
@@ -196,7 +196,9 @@


   /* support for Universal Windows Platform UWP, formerly WinRT */
-#ifdef _WINRT_DLL
+#if defined( _WINRT_DLL )                     ||                       \
+    ( defined( WINAPI_FAMILY_PARTITION )      &&                       \
+      !WINAPI_FAMILY_PARTITION( WINAPI_PARTITION_DESKTOP ) )

 #define PACK_DWORD64( hi, lo )  ( ( (DWORD64)(hi) << 32 ) | (DWORD)(lo) )

